A Republican sweep was all but assured today.  

Not because of how bad polling is. Not because of how bad Dem candidates are.  Not because of how easily betting markets are manipulated.  Nor because of how broken economic sentiment trackers are.  

It’s because this admin has a plan. 

This admin is aware that we are at a pivotal juncture in the history of this country. 

We have to get AI right.  

We have to decouple from China. Not the U.S. from China. The collective west has to be torn away completely.  

We need to crush Canada to show the Europeans what it costs to step out of line.  

We need to re-industrialize *before* robotics starts to ramp. 

We need to regime change Iran *before* drones become a lot more lethal with onboard AI. 

We need to regime change left-leaning South American countries *before* Europe attempts to say no when we force them to decouple from China.  

And if Trump is a lame duck for two years navigating any of this will be impossible.  

And because the actions that lead to the current point are only rational if there is a decoupling plan at the end of all this the only conclusion one can make is that the admin is far more sanguine about today’s results than literally everyone else. 

And because wall st is terrible at framing and betting on unquantifiable scenarios.  

And because I have closely observed how the pollsters and pundits have attempted to model elections.  

And because I understand the economic divergence that has occurred between Dems and repubs under this admin. 

I feel perfectly comfortable putting my reputation on the line.  

Because if I’m wrong I’m not just wrong about elections.  I’m probably also wrong about the strategic capacity of the current admin.  

And if they didn’t put sufficient thought into navigating the midterms all is lost anyways. 

Republican sweep.  Decoupling next.  Never blackpill.  

🫡

